    <bpmn:task id="Bridge_2_298d" name="Here are two options for a concise transition sentence connecting Process A and Process B, explaining how the outcome of A triggers B:&#10;&#10;**Option 1 (Focus on Financial Trigger):**&#10;&gt; Following the successful invoicing and payment received from the subsidiary order in Process A, the funds can be allocated to operational expenses, such as those required to run the restaurant in Process B.&#10;&#10;**Option 2 (Focus on Goods Trigger):**&#10;&gt; The goods shipped and invoiced in Process A (e.g., food supplies) could be delivered to the restaurant, enabling the preparation of meals for guests in Process B once they arrive and order." /><bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_P2B_2" sourceRef="atom_1_sid-62B31769-8A18-49B7-B397-18BBAEB6F5FC" targetRef="Bridge_2_298d" /><bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_B2C_2" sourceRef="Bridge_2_298d" targetRef="atom_2_Task_1" /><bpmn:task id="atom_3_Task_1" name="Create content">
